args: stale
exit: 0
--- stdout ---
longterm-mem: stale: 1 observations in current-name, checked against <project>
  nothing this repository disagrees with
--- stderr ---
longterm-mem: stale: --project not given, adopted "current-name" from the working directory (the memory already lives under this name; derived via the declared rule)
WARN stale: "former-name" also hold memory and are the same repository as "current-name"; they are owed an integration into it. longterm-mem reads Engram read-only and must not merge it: run `engram projects consolidate` to fold them in.
--- ledger ---
{
  "schema": "longterm-mem.identity-ledger/v1",
  "revision": "<digest>",
  "entries": [
    {
      "name": "<project>/.git",
      "rule": "common_dir",
      "adoptable": true,
      "first_seen": "<run>",
      "last_seen": "<run>"
    },
    {
      "name": "checkout",
      "rule": "directory",
      "adoptable": false,
      "first_seen": "<run>",
      "last_seen": "<run>"
    },
    {
      "name": "current-name",
      "rule": "declared",
      "adoptable": true,
      "first_seen": "<run>",
      "last_seen": "<run>"
    },
    {
      "name": "former-name",
      "rule": "declared",
      "adoptable": true,
      "first_seen": "2020-01-01T00:00:00Z",
      "last_seen": "2020-01-01T00:00:00Z"
    }
  ]
}
